Usage: axe <url...> [options]

Options:
  -V, --version                 output the version number
  -i, --include <list>          CSS selector of included elements, comma
                                separated
  -e, --exclude <list>          CSS selector of excluded elements, comma
                                separated
  -r, --rules <list>            IDs of rules to run, comma separated
  -t, --tags <list>             Tags of rules to run, comma separated
  -l, --disable <list>          IDs of rules to disable, comma separated
  -b, --browser [browser-name]  Which browser to run (Webdriver required)
  -s, --save [filename]         Save the output as a JSON file. Filename is
                                optional
  -j, --stdout                  Output results to STDOUT and silence all other
                                output
  -d, --dir <path>              Output directory
  -a, --axe-source <path>       Path to axe.js file
  -q, --exit                    Exit with `1` failure code if any a11y tests
                                fail
  -v, --verbose                 Output metadata like test tool name, version
                                and environment
  --load-delay <n>              Set how much time (milliseconds) axe will wait
                                after page load before running the audit
                                (default: 0)
  --timeout <n>                 Set how much time (seconds) axe has to run
                                (default: "90")
  --timer                       Log the time it takes to run
  --show-errors [boolean]       Display the full error stack (default: true)
  --no-reporter                 Turn the CLI reporter off
  --chrome-options [options]    Options to provide to headless Chrome
  --chromedriver-path <path>    Absolute path to the desired chromedriver
                                executable
  --chrome-path <path>          Path to the desired chrome executable
  -h, --help                    display help for command
